---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { href } from "../../data/site";
---
<Base title="Studies" description="Grain-production questions taken through the orchestra: early sowing of wheat on open trial data, and nitrogen topdressing of barley on a synthetic copy of confidential GRDC trials." path="/examples">
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">Studies through the orchestra</p>
      <h1>Studies</h1>
      <p class="prose lead mt-2">Each study takes one grain-production question from the data to a decision a grower can
        act on. Where the data are open, the analysis runs on the real records and reports the true effect, with the R
        code to run it again. Where the data are confidential, the plan is written and rehearsed on a synthetic copy,
        and only the copy's numbers are shown here.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <a class="card ex-card" href={href("/examples/sowing-time")}>
        <p class="kicker">Open trial data · NSW and Queensland, 2008 to 2017</p>
        <h2 class="ex-card-h">Does wheat sown earlier yield more?</h2>
        <p class="muted mt-2">Early sowing gained 0.22 t/ha (0.06 to 0.39), worth $58/ha at $261/t. The average gain is
          positive with 98% probability. R script included.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="card ex-card" href={href("/examples/nitrogen-topdressing")}>
        <p class="kicker">Confidential GRDC trials · synthetic copy only</p>
        <h2 class="ex-card-h">How much nitrogen to topdress in June?</h2>
        <p class="muted mt-2">With a known response planted in the copy, the orchestra found it: 2.05 t/ha (1.94 to 2.15)
          from 90 kg N/ha, against the planted 2.07, and a rate that follows soil moisture as planted.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
